
 Filter ->
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 You use Filter to extract information from an incoming message. In other words, you filter out parts of the
 message that you do not want and extract only the data that you want.
 -> The Filter component is used to evaluate conditions and selectively route or process messages based on
    specified criteria.
    It enables conditional routing or filtering of messages within an integration flow.

    config :  (General, Processing)

    General :  Name
    Processing :

    XPath Expression (ET) :
    -> Specify Xpath to the message node that contains information to be extracted

  Value Type (DD) :  (String,Integer,Boolean,Node,Nodelist)

   ->  specify the value extract from the xml

      String-  The output of filter is of type string
      Integer- The output of filter is of type integer
      Boolean - The output of filter is of type boolean
      Node - The output of filter is of type node
      Nodelist - The output of filter is a collection of nodes.




